  "description": "TAFBOU crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C214 H298 Gd4 Mn4 N6 O38,6(C3 H7 N1 O1),4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.563-3.978 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.64-111.33°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C236H356N12O48Mn4Gd4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Mn(III), Gd(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
